cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "munch"
abstract: >-
  A C++23 lexing library that builds a lexer at runtime from regex combinators: a combinator AST, Thompson
  construction into an NFA, subset construction and minimization into a DFA, and a Builder/Lexer orchestration layer
  on top. It also derives certified split symbols from the compiled automaton, bytes at which every occurrence in a
  completely tokenizable input begins a token, so an input can be divided and scanned in parallel with the token
  stream preserved exactly, without speculation or a merge phase. For bytes occurring in some completely tokenizable
  input, the condition is necessary as well as sufficient once the analysis is restricted to states an input can reach
  and from which acceptance is still reachable.
keywords:
  - lexical analysis
  - tokenization
  - deterministic finite automata
  - maximal munch
  - parallel lexing
  - C++
